Notebook[{
Cell["Transformation of a black-box unitary (Sect. 7.4, eqs. (170)-(178), Table 2). Optimal deterministic sequential superchannel (quantum comb) with n calls to an unknown U in U(d) that implements f(U) = U^T or U^{-1}. The comb is parametrised by the matrix units of A^d_{p,q} (eq. (177)): use {p,q} = {n,1} for U^T and {p,q} = {n+1,0} for U^{-1}. Requires idempotents/metadata_p_q_d.m, idempotents/elementary_p_q_d.m and blocks/blocks_*_d.m, produced by compute_matrix_units_and_blocks.nb. Normalisation: Tr C = d^(n+1). Expected optimal fidelities (Table 2): U^T d=2: 0.5, 0.75, 0.933013, 1; d=3: 0.222222, 0.407407, 0.626597, 0.799250; U^{-1} d=2: as U^T; d=3: 0.222222, 0.333333, 0.444444, 0.555556 (n = 1..4). The exact d = 2, n = 4 transposition protocol is in guess_magic_4_1_2.nb.", "Text"],

